<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-April non-CIS nickel exports jump yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-April non-CIS nickel exports jump yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia exported 67,400 tonnes of nickel to countries outside the Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) in the first four months of 1997, up 37 percent from year-ago levels, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Non-CIS primary aluminium exports edged up two percent year-on-year in the first four months to 880,100 tonnes, while copper rose eight percent to 182,600 tonnes, Interfax news agency quoted the committee as saying.</p>
<p>The committee gave the following figures --</p>
<p>RUSSIAN JAN-APRIL 1997 NON-CIS BASE METALS EXPORTS (TONNES)</p>
<p>		     Jan-April	 Jan-April	 pct</p>
<p>			 1997		1996	   change</p>
<p> aluminium	 880,100	   863,100	    +2</p>
<p> copper	    182,600	   168,800	    +8</p>
<p> nickel	     67,400	    49,200	   +37</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
